# raycontrol (public) for .github/workflows/raycontrol-interop.yml: the commit whose rayd the client is checked against.
REPOSITORY_RAYCONTROL="https://github.com/arngory/raycontrol.git"
# v0.31.2 (niko-server v0.18.2 in its VERSIONS: the Hysteria2 server's keepalive 28 s, the UDP front against spoofed
# floods, forged confirmations and reflection; raycontrol's own code as in v0.31.0 but for its release workflow;
# v0.31.1 was not released). Since v0.31.0 (quic-cid-route-v1: the front takes a QUIC client whose address changed (a new NAT port, a new socket) to
# the same backend, nothing for the client to change; Hysteria2 checks a client's new path before sending on it;
# `rayctl device revoke -overlap` replaces a device on a schedule, the user's credentials rotated as planned rather
# than at once; niko-server v0.18.0, whose front drops fake Initials and reads the ClientHello of Initials in any
# order on every UDP route by name. Manual interop run 43992797892 on 3e9828b with niko-server v0.18.0: all three
# jobs green, the naive QUIC desync checks among them). Since v0.30.0 (naive-udp-v1: UDP through naive as HTTP/3 datagrams where the line says udp=1, the probe of a network
# through a datagram request at the probe name, off by default; code of 157c943, which interop runs 43875186505 and
# 43883398436 checked: TestRaycontrolNaiveUDP and its in-process probe). Since v0.29.0 (R4-42: naive's name changes by epochs and on the operator's command, the new one in the profile's next, the
# same line with another sni and the same niko-pin; the front serves the new name ahead and the old ones after, over
# h2 and QUIC; interop run 43750635660 on d8b8236, whose code this is: TestRaycontrolNaiveSNI). Since v0.28.1
# (hardening after fuzzing: rayspa refuses a perimeter snapshot of another port protocol than tcp/udp and a
# relay bundle with a zone in its exit address, numbers over 16 bits are no longer cut; RelayUpdateStatus.error says
# why a relay's install failed, up to 200 bytes; interop run 43702018075 on 1f095f2, whose tree this is). Since v0.28.0
# relay-update-remote-v1: a node's relays follow its version one at a time where their root allows it, and
# GetUpdateStatus lists them; a new user's DoH tokens taken at once. Since v0.27.0 a device revoked renews its user's credentials, RenewUser; a DoH token per device; the
# node's own outbound TLS on its embedded roots, extra ones through rayd serve -tls-roots; the REALITY target option;
# latest_patch, GetPorts. Since v0.26.0 the site's key pins (cert-pin-v1), honest connect in rayd naive, rayctl for
# macOS and FreeBSD; its Xray fork at 46b58d4; per-user connection limits since v0.25.0; Register again with the same
# key, a key switch within the grace refused unless forced and naive's 429 since v0.24.0; lan-v1 since v0.23.0, the
# traffic limit since v0.22.0, icmp-v1, the node's note and niko-ack=1 since v0.21.0, each device its own Yggdrasil key
# since v0.20.1, UDP through naive since v0.20.0; niko-server v0.18.0 and slipstream-server server-v0.2.0 in its
# VERSIONS). Its SHA256SUMS signed with the release key the server session checks, the tag on this commit
COMMIT_RAYCONTROL="02a69b32ef05e9b3ec11172ca43f5c118acf011e"
# NaiveProxy's own client, a release of klzgrad's: the reference client of the naive job. The app's library is
# another build, Chromium 158 from arngory/cronet-go (libcore/go.mod)
NAIVE_CHROMIUM="154.0.8037.49"
